    "scenarioText": "Always passionate about two-wheelers, Indushekhar, supported by his father \nMahesh Shekhar, his uncle Chandrashekhar and also by some other close \nrelatives incorporated a company by the name SpeedWheels Limited way back \nin 1990. Its Registered Office was situated in Lucknow, and it manufactured \nvariety of scooters in the range of 110CC to 160CC and motorcycles from 100CC \nto 200CC and 400CC. Slowly and gradually, SpeedWheels Limited started \nexporting its vehicles and in the course of time, it became one of the leading \nnames in the country as well as in European and African countries. In 2020, \nIndushekhar’s twins Anirudh and Dhanush joined him in managing the \nflourishing business while Indushekhar’s father Mahesh Shekhar and his uncle \nChandrashekhar stepped down as directors due to the advancing age. \nThe management team of SpeedWheels Limited then comprised as under which \ncontinues to be so: \nS. \nNo. \nName Designation \n1. Indushekhar \nChairman and Managing Director \n(CMD) \n2. Anirudh, elder son of \nIndushekhar \nDirector (Finance and Accounts) \n3. Dhanush, younger son of \nIndushekhar \nWhole-time Director (WTD) \n4. \nSrilakshmi, wife of \nIndushekhar \nDirector (Human Resources and other \nMiscellaneous Departments) \n5. Divyanshi, daughter of \nIndushekhar \nDirector (Marketing) \n6. Sambhavie Company Secretary \n7. Dipankarr Independent Director \n8. Rudraa Pratap Independent Director \nThough motorcycles are undoubtedly a thrilling way to travel, offering freedom \nand adventure with every ride but with the entry of young twins of Indushekhar \n\n28 \n\ncame new vistas to manufacture sports bikes. The manufacturing of sports bikes \nwould definitely mean a bike to handle sharp turns, high speeds and aggressive \nriding. Keeping this fact in view both the brothers thoroughly discussed the \nmanufacturing of sports bikes with their father Indushekhar who \nwholeheartedly accepted the proposal. It was decided that these would be \nlight-weight, aerodynamic and equipped with powerful engines that would give \nroom for rapid acceleration and top speed. This project soon got speed and the \ndemand for sports bikes saw great acceleration in the market. \nThe overall business was flourishing by leaps and bounds. In continuation, some \nof the important figures extracted from the audited Balance Sheet of \nSpeedWheels Limited (as at March 31, 2025) are as under: \nS. \nNo. \nParticulars \nAmount \n(in crore) \n1. Authorised Share Capital (divided into 5 crore equity \nshares of ` 10 each) \n50 \n2. Paid-up Share Capital 48 \n3. Net worth 128 \n4. Remaining Term Loan from Star Commercial Bank Ltd. 20 \n5. Non-current Assets 64 \n6. Turnover 9,500 \nSeeing good results especially of the new product, the confidence of the twins \nreached the next level. Dhanush is now desirous of making overseas direct \ninvestment (ODI) in Automotive Bikes Manufacturing Co. Ltd. based at United \nKingdom (U.K.). In fact, about six months before, he had met Richards, a director \nin Automotive Bikes Manufacturing Co. Ltd. at Singapore where a Seminar was \nbeing held by the Techno Chamber of Commerce and Industry, Singapore. \nHaving similar interests, both Dhanush and Richards developed a strong bond, \nand it was agreed between them that SpeedWheels Limited would invest a \nsizeable amount by purchasing fresh equity shares of Automotive Bikes \nManufacturing Co. Ltd. \nAbout a month before, SpeedWheels Limited received an advance payment of \nUSD 50,000 from United Motors & Dealers AB of Sweden against supply of 200 \nsports bikes. This deal culminated because of the vigorous efforts of Divyanshi, \n\nDirector (Marketing), who could convince her similar counterpart Elias, Director \n(Marketing) of United Motors & Dealers regarding the superiority of her \ncompany’s product. \nAnirudh, Director (Finance and Accounts), had a friend Smith from his college \ndays who after completing his studies in India had shifted to Czech Republic in \nCentral Europe. Anirudh sent him a bottle of ‘Misty Petal Perfume’ as a gift on \nhis first wedding anniversary. For this purpose, he simply made a declaration \nthat the ‘Misty Petal Perfume’ was being exported by way of gift and its value \nwas ` 1,32,000 only. He did not make any declaration in one of the specified \nforms set out in the Export of Goods and Services Regulations, 2015 as is usually \nrequired in the case of export of goods. \nFor travelling on new roads, SpeedWheels Limited is planning to launch a new \nassembly facility in Nepal in partnership with Omkar Motors Limited. Dhanush \nwas entrusted to finalise the Agreement between his company and Omkar \nMotors. However, before finalisation, Dhanush instructed Sambhavie to visit \nNepal to take stock of as to how the new assembly facility will function in future. \nIt is worth noting that the proposed facility at Nepal would have a capacity to \nproduce about 50,000 units per year and the said joint venture would also result \nin creating sizeable job opportunities for the unemployed youth in Nepal. \nSambhavie estimated to take USD 4,000 to Nepal for her forthcoming visit and \nfor this purpose she approached her banker National Commercial Bank to \nwithdraw the foreign exchange.",
