    "scenarioText": "Close friends from school days having similar tastes, Padmaja and Ambuja \njoined a forward-thinking international school, namely, TopRung American \nInternational School, Chennai, which is a part of Marie Education Trust, founded \nby Chairman Benjamin, as post-graduate teachers (PGT-Science). During their \nteaching careers, both of them came in contact with Adharshila Foundation, a \nSection 8 company, focusing on uplifting children living on the fringes of society \nby educating them and providing health-care services. NGO Adharshila \nFoundation holds Certificate of Registration under the Foreign Contribution \n(Regulation) Act, 2010 and receives foreign contributions from different \ncountries. \nComing to Padamja and Ambuja, they, invariably, on weekends except when \nthere existed some emergency requiring their urgent presence somewhere else, \nstarted going to Adharshila Foundation as volunteers to provide their humble \nand sincere services to the needy children. This used to be a satisfying \nexperience for both of them. Soon, father of Padmaja i.e. Murli Krishnan, (who \nretired some seven years back as Vice President from Nirmal Tech Limited), \njoined them too. \nFinding this new journey of life, a soul-satisfying phenomenon, Murli Krishnan \nalong with two of his close friends of similar age, Swaminathan and Abhinavan \n(retired as Joint Secretaries from Ministry of Civil Aviation) decided to use their \ncombined experience to make a greater difference and impact on society. These \ntwo friends of Murali Krishnan were also very much interested in contributing \ntheir might for this noble cause; and all of them, therefore, thought of \nincorporating a Section 8 company in August 2018 by the name ‘Beyond \nHorizons’. \nAfter its incorporation and obtaining a licence under Section 8, Beyond \nHorizons started working as a charitable organisation with a trajectory to keep \nan eye on rural development by giving a new purpose to unused fabrics and \nused clothes of all the sizes that were usually collected from urban areas and \nthe company started distributing them in nearby rural areas. An account was \nopened in Punjab National Bank, Teynampet in Chennai. Several others joined \n\n46 \n\nthem in due course of time. Their intention was to be as self-sustainable as \npossible, whether that would be through in-house fundraising events or \nthrough generous support from the corporate partners. \nBy the end of the Financial Year 2023-24, the capital fund of Beyond Horizons, \nmainly comprising of contributions from wealthy individuals and philanthropic \norganisations, had reached ` one crore. By now, Padamja and Ambuja had \nstarted helping Beyond Horizons, though unofficially, in enhancing its \nphilanthropic activities. \nIt is noteworthy that in the month of May 2023, Beyond Horizons received the \nCertificate of Registration issued under the Foreign Contribution (Regulation) \nAct, 2010 as the company expected to receive foreign contributions from two \norganisations located at Switzerland and United Kingdom. Vibhavari, mother of \nPadmaja and wife of Murli Krishnan (who retired from Ministry of Finance in \nFebruary 2025) also formally joined Beyond Horizons. In March 2025, Beyond \nHorizons with the coordinated efforts of its directors received foreign \ncontribution to the extent of USD 40,000 from the philanthropic organisation \nof Switzerland. In order to boost the income of Beyond Horizons, the directors, \nin particular, Murli Krishnan and his wife Vibhavari are contemplating investing \na portion of the foreign contribution in renowned mutual funds. \nOf late, it was noticed that Adharshila Foundation, which holds the Certificate \nof Registration under Foreign Contribution (Regulation) Act, 2010, for the \nreasons known to it, has not been engaged in any reasonable activity in its \nchosen field for the benefit of society.",
