    "scenarioText": "Banyan Tree Enterprises Pvt. Ltd., incorporated in India for the past 6 years, has \nnot conducted any business operations or significant financial transactions for \nthe last two consecutive financial years (FY 2023-24 and 2024-25). The company \ndid not file financial statements or annual returns for these two years, stating \nminimal activity. \nDespite inactivity, Banyan Tree continued paying statutory fees to the Registrar \nof Companies (RoC) and paid rent for maintaining its office and accounting \nrecords regularly during the past two years. The directors now plan to apply to \nthe RoC for the company to be declared a dormant company under Section 455 \nof the Companies Act, 2013, to reduce regulatory compliance requirements. \nAdditional facts: \n• There is no pending legal dispute or management conflict. \n• The company has no loans, outstanding statutory dues, or workmen dues. \n• However, an investigation was initiated against Banyan Tree six months \nago, which is currently in progress but no report has been concluded. \n• The directors ask whether a special resolution in the general meeting is \nrequired before making the dormant status application. \nAnswer the given questions in the light of the Companies Act, 2013",
