    "scenarioText": "XYZ Ltd., a technology manufacturing company, plans to raise funds through \nan Initial Public Offer (IPO). The company files its Draft Red Herring Prospectus \n(DRHP) with SEBI and the stock exchanges. The key facts are as follows: \n• XYZ Ltd. has applied for in-principle approval for listing its shares on BSE \nand NSE, designating NSE as the lead exchange. \n• It has entered into an agreement with NSDL for dematerialization. \nHowever, 10% of promoter shareholding is still in physical form. \n• The company had earlier issued partly paid-up shares; out of these, 5% \nremain partly paid at the time of DRHP filing. \n• The IPO proposes to raise ` 2,000 crore, of which: \n ` 1,000 crore will be used for project expansion. \n ` 600 crore is earmarked for investment in a target company (yet to \nbe finalized). \n ` 300 crore is stated for “general corporate purposes.” \n ` 100 crore is allocated for debt repayment. \n• Financially, XYZ Ltd. was earlier a partnership firm until April 2022 and \nconverted into a company in May 2022. Its financial statements for FY \n2020–22 of the partnership business were restated in the format \nprescribed under the Companies Act, 2013 and duly certified by statutory \nauditors in compliance with accounting standards. \nAnswer the following question as per the applicable provisions of the \nSEBI(ICDR) Regulations, 2018: \n\n66",
