    "scenarioText": "Apex Ventures Ltd. (Acquirer), along with its Persons Acting in Concert (PACs), held 23% of the equity shares carrying voting rights in Horizon Infra Ltd. (a listed Target Company on NSE and BSE) as on 31st March 2025. On 15th July 2025, Apex Ventures Ltd. acquired an additional 3% voting rights in Horizon Infra Ltd. through open market purchases, taking its aggregate shareholding to 26%.\n\nSeparately, in another listed company, Sterling Pharma Ltd., the promoter group already held 38% of the voting rights as on 1st April 2025. During FY 2025-26, the promoter group acquired 4% additional shares in July 2025 and now wishes to acquire another 2.5% shares in January 2026 (within the same financial year) without triggering a mandatory open offer. Meanwhile, an intermediary aggrieved by an adjudication order passed by a SEBI Adjudicating Officer under Section 15-I of the SEBI Act, 1992 wishes to prefer an appeal before the Securities Appellate Tribunal (SAT) under Section 15T.",
